---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { asOf, days } from "../lib/data.ts";
import { breadcrumbLd, countLine } from "../lib/seo.ts";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site.ts";
---

<Base
  title={`About · ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`${SITE.name} puts one brilliant and one baffling true story from the United States side by side, every day. ${SITE.tagline}`}
  path="/about"
  ogImage="/og/about.png"
  ogImageAlt="About"
  modified={asOf}
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbLd([{ name: "About", path: "/about" }])]}
>
  <div class="day-head">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="tagline">{SITE.tagline}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      In the same news cycle, someone in America wins a Nobel Prize for a new way of editing DNA and
      someone else in America marries a tree. Both are true. Both are reported by serious
      newspapers. They sit three stories apart on the same front page, and nobody comments on the
      distance between them.
    </p>
    <p>
      This site does nothing but measure that distance. Every day it finds one story that shows what
      people in this country are capable of, and one that shows what they are also capable of, and
      puts them next to each other. There is no commentary. The content speaks for itself, and
      readers make up their own minds.
    </p>
    <p>
      The pair is found and checked automatically, with rules that are stricter than most
      newsrooms': two independent accepted publishers per story, an adversarial second review, and
      verbatim quotes matched against the live pages. The <a href="/methodology">methodology</a>{" "}
      explains all of it, and the <a href="/log">scan log</a> shows every candidate that was
      considered and why it was or wasn't published. So far: {countLine(days)}.
    </p>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is independent and automated. It takes no money from any publisher or party, runs
      no comments, and sets no cookies. The code and every published day live in a public repository
      at <a href={SITE.repoUrl}>GitHub</a>. Headlines and summaries are licensed{" "}
      <a href={SITE.license.url}>{SITE.license.name}</a>; the articles it links to belong to their
      publishers.
    </p>
    <p>
      Made by <a href="https://paulblandfilms.com">Paul Bland</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
